      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There are many potential outcomes or endpoints to choose from to assess the effects of asthma treatments, and a wide range of such measures are used in different trials. This can make it difficult to compare treatment outcomes from different trials and to understand whether new treatments offer a genuine clinical benefit for patients. Here we review the common endpoints used in trials to assess the efficacy of asthma treatments."},
      "ArticleTitle": "Endpoints in asthma drug trials--what do they mean?",
